@@ -15,3 +15,15 @@ resolvePointer(doc, ""); // the whole document
 
 `resolvePointer` throws a `JsonPointerError` when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer, or when it does
 not resolve to a value of the document (missing member, out-of-range index, `-`, descending into a scalar).
+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyPatch({ a: [1] }, [{ op: "add", path: "/a/-", value: 2 }]); // { a: [1, 2] }
+```
+
+`applyPatch` applies the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` in order and
+returns the result as a new value; the document and the patch are not mutated. It throws a
+`JsonPatchError` when the patch is invalid or an operation fails (including a failed `test`).
