+## Why
+
+Services need to change JSON documents with standard patches. The library implements RFC 6901 pointers but has no way to apply RFC 6902 JSON Patch.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)` implementing RFC 6902 (`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`).
+- Export it, and a `JsonPatchError`, from `src/index.ts`.
+- The input document and patch are never mutated; a new document is returned.
+- Document the feature in the README.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying RFC 6902 JSON Patch documents to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+New `src/json-patch.ts` and tests; `src/index.ts` and `README.md` updated. Reuses pointer parsing from `src/json-pointer.ts`.
